    "updated_at": "2026-11-27T11:28:33Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 470d1a27c. No code change is necessary. Evidence:\n\n1. `cut.yml`: the two jobs use `runs-on: [self-hosted, camcraft-cut]` (lines 65 and 151). Commit afde91109 (PR #3254) made this change.\n2. `runners` skill: the section \"The cut runner (#1413)\" already gives the `camcraft-cut` label, says that only the cut runner has it, and gives the reason (#3253). The skill text agrees with `cut.yml`.\n3. skull and egg: the reason to keep them out of the post-merge pool was #3258. #3258 is closed (2026-11-22T07:27:55Z, shipped in v0.26.0). Thus this part has no more reason.\n\nOne part stays, and it is not code. A person with admin access to the runners must add the label `camcraft-cut` to the cut runner (Settings -> Actions -> Runners). Until then, a `cut.yml` run waits in the queue. An agent cannot read or change the runner labels (the runners API gives HTTP 403).\n\nSuggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
